cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Detection limits for lunar water ice in Chandrayaan-2 DFSAR
  compact-polarimetric data: analysis code and verification gates
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the
  accompanying paper. The satellite source products are not part of this
  software and carry separate terms; see DATA.md.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Saksham
    family-names: Raina
    affiliation: "Marathwada Mitra Mandal's Institute of Technology, Pune, India"
    email: sakshamraina16@gmail.com
  - given-names: Ayushi
    family-names: Raina
    affiliation: "Cornell University, Ithaca, NY, USA"
  - given-names: Piyush
    family-names: Pandey
    affiliation: "Marathwada Mitra Mandal's Institute of Technology, Pune, India"
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Sakshamraina07/LunarIceIntelligence'
abstract: >-
  Code, derived artifacts and verification gates for a study of the
  detection limits of a CPR-based lunar water-ice criterion applied
  to a single Chandrayaan-2 DFSAR L-band pass over the lunar south
  pole. Contains no Chandrayaan-2 or LOLA source products and no layer,
  tile or screenshot rendering a DFSAR-derived quantity at a pixel size
  finer than 200 m, with two stated exceptions (DATA.md): a 125 m per
  pixel delta-DOP map on GitHub that is not in the release archive, and
  one panel of a manuscript figure at 25 m bins. It holds code, derived
  numerical results, figures, coarse aggregate layers (about 200 m and
  coarser) and LOLA-only map layers. ISRO keeps the copyright in the
  Chandrayaan-2 data. Every figure and number is regenerated from
  products obtained separately from PRADAN and the NASA PDS.
keywords:
  - synthetic aperture radar
  - compact polarimetry
  - equivalent number of looks
  - detection statistics
  - lunar water ice
  - Moon
  - planetary radar
  - speckle
license: MIT
